    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together in the math lab, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their working schedules. Each person works on a different schedule:\n\n- Darren works every 3 school days.\n- Wanda works every 4 school days.\n- Beatrice works every 6 school days.\n- Chi works every 7 school days.\n\nThe least common multiple of these numbers is the smallest positive integer that is a multiple of each of them. We will calculate the LCM step by step.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of each number:\n- The prime factorization of 3 is \\(3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 4 is \\(2^2\\).\n- The prime factorization of 6 is \\(2 \\times 3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\(2^2\\).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\(3\\).\n- The highest power of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nTherefore, the LCM is:\n\\[\n2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n\\]\n\nSo, the least common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7 is 84. This means that Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together in the math lab in \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days.",
